[94.47, "o", "GILty 0.1.0 on AMD EPYC 7571, Python 3.13.16\r\nlearned Moby-Dick in 0.2 s: 212,796 words, 33,089 states\r\nEPYC 7571        1,140,633 words/s | I’ll clear it; they stood in the eddying again stooping a co\r\nEPYC 7571        1,286,354 words/s | Now, then, and plaster—tied to the prairie, in such a very c\r\n"]
[98.901, "o", "EPYC 7571        1,293,127 words/s | … men feel another separate these Orientals do heroes, saint\r\n"]
[103.937, "o", "EPYC 7571        1,295,184 words/s | As I then knocking off shore, eh? Nothing but upon the priso\r\n"]
[103.937, "o", "^C"]
[108.209, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[3J\u001b[H"]
[108.209, "m", "Let Spare Cores pick"]
[108.259, "o", "\u001b[2;3;36m# Same budget, measured data: the fastest single core (Geekbench 6) with a fast cache (at least 30,000\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[108.309, "o", "\u001b[2;3;36m# MB/s of single-threaded cached reads, PassMark), for no more than the r5a.large costs today:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[108.359, "o", "\u001b[2;3;36m# $0.1266/h, Auto Mode fee included. No Karpenter label can say any of this.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
